Key Functions of a Robot Chassis1. Structural Support & Mounting BaseActs as the main skeleton that holds the Arduino, L298N motor driver, HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor, and battery pack securely in place.  Prevents exposed wires and circuit boards from shorting out against loose parts.2. Mobility & Drivetrain AlignmentHouses the DC motors, wheels, and caster wheel (or omnidirectional wheel) in a fixed geometry.Ensures the drive wheels remain parallel and properly aligned so the robot moves straight without veering unexpectedly.3. Weight & Load DistributionEvenly distributes the weight of heavy components—like the external battery pack—over the wheels.Proper weight distribution prevents tipping over when accelerating, stopping abruptly, or making sharp turns.4. Component ProtectionShields delicate electronic modules from direct collisions with obstacles or floor debris during navigation.5. Ground Clearance & StabilitySets the height of the robot above the ground, allowing it to navigate smooth surfaces or minor bumps without scraping the bottom components.
